{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Craftimals: Build to the Sun",
    "steam_appid": 3172430,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<i>Craftimals: Build to the Sun</i> is the return of a classic! Originally an Xbox Live Indie Game fan favorite, this relaxing sandbox platformer combines simple block-stacking with adorable animal characters on a journey straight to the sky.<br><br>\ud83e\uddf1 Use intuitive building mechanics to construct your own path<br><br>\ud83d\udc3e Team up in 2-player local co-op or go it alone<br><br>\ud83c\udf1e Reach checkpoints to unlock new powers, cute hats, and other surprises<br><br>\ud83c\udfa8 Place blocks freely (no grids, no limits) and build in any direction<br><br>Whether you're chasing the sun, creating sky-high art, or just enjoying some stress-free platforming, <i>Craftimals</i> is a wholesome experience for all ages.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><br>\ud83e\udde9 Easy-to-learn building with satisfying vertical progression<br><br>\ud83d\udc6f\u200d\u2642\ufe0f Local 2-player, split screen co-op<br><br>\ud83c\udfb5 New soundtrack by Audionautix<br><br>\ud83e\udde2 Hats (so many hats)<br><br>\ud83d\udd8c\ufe0f Creative freedom in a giant, open canvas<br><br>\ud83c\udfc6 Steam achievements and leaderboards<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >What's New (and What's Not)</h2><br>This is a faithful PC port of the 2012 original, now updated with keyboard/mouse support and some modern Steam perks.<br><br>If you're looking for a more advanced evolution of this idea, then check out our other game, <i>Doggo Dig Down</i>, which is the spiritual successor to <i>Craftimals</i>.",
    "about_the_game": "<i>Craftimals: Build to the Sun</i> is the return of a classic! Originally an Xbox Live Indie Game fan favorite, this relaxing sandbox platformer combines simple block-stacking with adorable animal characters on a journey straight to the sky.<br><br>\ud83e\uddf1 Use intuitive building mechanics to construct your own path<br><br>\ud83d\udc3e Team up in 2-player local co-op or go it alone<br><br>\ud83c\udf1e Reach checkpoints to unlock new powers, cute hats, and other surprises<br><br>\ud83c\udfa8 Place blocks freely (no grids, no limits) and build in any direction<br><br>Whether you're chasing the sun, creating sky-high art, or just enjoying some stress-free platforming, <i>Craftimals</i> is a wholesome experience for all ages.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><br>\ud83e\udde9 Easy-to-learn building with satisfying vertical progression<br><br>\ud83d\udc6f\u200d\u2642\ufe0f Local 2-player, split screen co-op<br><br>\ud83c\udfb5 New soundtrack by Audionautix<br><br>\ud83e\udde2 Hats (so many hats)<br><br>\ud83d\udd8c\ufe0f Creative freedom in a giant, open canvas<br><br>\ud83c\udfc6 Steam achievements and leaderboards<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >What's New (and What's Not)</h2><br>This is a faithful PC port of the 2012 original, now updated with keyboard/mouse support and some modern Steam perks.<br><br>If you're looking for a more advanced evolution of this idea, then check out our other game, <i>Doggo Dig Down</i>, which is the spiritual successor to <i>Craftimals</i>.",
    "short_description": "Build your way to the sun in this cozy, creative sandbox platformer! Stack blocks, unlock powers, wear silly hats, and play solo or in 2-player couch co-op.",
    "supported_languages": "English",
    "reviews": "\u201cWhy does continuously building higher and higher result in fun? I couldn't tell you, but I had a really hard time prying myself away from this game.\u201d<br>Kotaku<br><br>\u201cSometimes, it's not about winning the game, it's how you play. Craftimals: Build to the Sun embodies that message in an adorable little package.\u201d<br>Freakin' Awesome Network<br>",
